    "Prioritize leg performance next period — aim to reverse the small strength index dip from 108 to 107 by ensuring leg sessions are fresh, well-fueled, and that load or reps are slightly increased on your primary leg movements.",
    "Add one additional set of direct biceps work to bring biceps volume more in line with triceps, supporting balanced arm development and healthier elbow joint loading over time.",
    "Continue the upward trend on chest and shoulders by applying small, consistent load increases — even adding one or two reps or a small weight increment will keep the strength index climbing.",
    "Maintain the current balance between chest, back, and shoulders, as the 26.8%, 28%, and 10.4% volume split reflects a solid push-pull structure — protect this balance as you make adjustments elsewhere."
  ],
  "contextSummary": "Upper body strength progressed well with chest and shoulders gaining index points; legs saw a minor dip from 108 to 107 that needs monitoring, and biceps volume remains low relative to overall balance."
}
